
<!--
TRIANGLE PROTOCOL（CLICK）
DESIGN INSPIRED BY Link：https://www.orvelumm.com/lab?utm_source
This website inspired my exploration of an experimental
digital interface and an immersive visual atmosphere.
I used it as a visual reference when developing the
direction of Triangle Protocol, while adapting the
design to suit my own memory-game concept and interaction.

Triangle Protocol is a browser-based memory reconstruction game. The
player observes a sequence of highlighted triangle nodes and then
repeats the same sequence by clicking the nodes in the correct order.
The fictional security-system theme gives this simple memory activity
a clear purpose: each completed level represents progress towards
restoring access to the system.

I organised the interface into an introduction screen and a separate
game screen. The introduction establishes the context before the player
starts interacting.  This separation is intended to make the first step clear 
and avoid presenting all the game information at once.

The HTML uses semantic elements such as header, main, section, aside
and footer to organise content into meaningful areas. Buttons are used
for actions because they are interactive controls, rather than using
ordinary text elements as clickable controls. The type="button"
attribute makes the intended button behaviour explicit.

The hidden attribute is used on the game screen and feedback overlays
so that these elements can be shown or hidden as the interaction
progresses. The JavaScript controls when the player moves between
screens and when error or success feedback becomes visible.

Accessibility was also considered. Labels such as aria-label provide
descriptions for interface elements where visual appearance alone may
not communicate their purpose. Decorative elements use aria-hidden="true" so that
they do not add unnecessary information to the accessibility tree.

The triangle shapes are generated through inline SVG in JavaScript,
rather than loaded from an external image library. The supplied HTML
does not reference third-party image, icon or audio assets. Therefore,
there are no external media creators or media licences to attribute
for the assets shown in this version.

-->

<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
  <title>Triangle Protocol</title>
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="style.css">
  <script src="script.js" defer></script>
</head>
<body>
  <header class="site-header">
    <a class="logo" href="#">TRIANGLE<span>_PROTOCOL</span></a>
    <div class="system-status">
      <span class="status-dot"></span>
      SYSTEM ONLINE
    </div>
  </header>

  <main class="main-container">

    <!-- FIRST SCREEN: INTRO -->
    <section class="intro-screen" id="intro-screen">
      <p class="eyebrow">MEMORY RECONSTRUCTION SYSTEM</p>

      <h1>Reconstruct the <span>sequence.</span></h1>

      <p class="intro-description">
        Observe the signal. Remember the pattern. Restore the system.
      </p>

      <div class="intro-decoration" aria-hidden="true">
        <span></span>
        <span></span>
        <span></span>
      </div>

      <p class="intro-instruction">
        A COGNITIVE MEMORY TEST // TP-07
      </p>

      <button class="system-unlock-button" id="system-unlock-button" type="button">
        UNLOCK THE SYSTEM
        <span aria-hidden="true">→</span>
      </button>

      <p class="intro-footer">INITIALISE THE INTERFACE TO CONTINUE</p>
    </section>

    <!-- SECOND SCREEN: GAME -->
    <section class="game-screen" id="game-screen" hidden>
      <div class="game-heading">
        <p class="eyebrow">NEURAL INTERFACE // TP-07</p>
        <h1>Memory <span>Protocol.</span></h1>
        <p class="intro-description">
          Observe the signal. Remember the pattern. Restore the system.
        </p>
      </div>

      <section class="game-layout" aria-label="Triangle memory game">

        <!-- LEFT PANEL -->
        <div class="matrix-panel">
          <div class="panel-top">
            <span>TRIANGLE INTERFACE</span>
            <span class="panel-indicator">● ACTIVE</span>
          </div>

          <section class="neural-hud" aria-label="Game status">
            <div class="hud-heading">
              <span class="hud-index" id="hud-index">01</span>
              <span class="hud-title">/ NEURAL MATRIX</span>
            </div>

            <div class="hud-grid">
              <div class="hud-item">
                <span class="hud-label">INPUT REQUIRED</span>
                <span class="hud-value" id="input-required">AWAITING INPUT</span>
              </div>

              <div class="hud-item">
                <span class="hud-label">SIGNAL STATUS</span>
                <span class="hud-value cyan" id="signal-status">STANDBY</span>
              </div>

              <div class="hud-item">
                <span class="hud-label">SECURITY LEVEL</span>
                <span class="hud-value cyan" id="security-level">01 / 07</span>
              </div>

              <div class="hud-item">
                <span class="hud-label">ACCESS MODE</span>
                <span class="hud-value" id="access-mode">STANDBY</span>
              </div>
            </div>
          </section>

          <div class="matrix-stage" id="matrix-stage">
            <div class="stage-grid" aria-hidden="true"></div>
            <div class="stage-corner corner-tl" aria-hidden="true"></div>
            <div class="stage-corner corner-tr" aria-hidden="true"></div>
            <div class="stage-corner corner-bl" aria-hidden="true"></div>
            <div class="stage-corner corner-br" aria-hidden="true"></div>

            <div class="matrix" id="matrix" aria-label="Triangle nodes"></div>

            <!-- Wrong answer overlay -->
            <div class="error-overlay" id="error-overlay" hidden>
              <div class="error-box" role="alert" aria-live="assertive">
                <span class="error-icon" aria-hidden="true">!</span>
                <div class="error-title">ACCESS LOCKED</div>
                <div class="error-description">SEQUENCE MISMATCH</div>
                <div class="error-subtext">REPLAYING SIGNAL...</div>
              </div>
            </div>

            <!-- Final success overlay -->
            <div class="success-overlay" id="success-overlay" hidden>
              <div class="success-box">
                <div class="success-icon" aria-hidden="true">✓</div>
                <p class="success-eyebrow">ALL SECURITY LEVELS VERIFIED</p>
                <h2>SYSTEM <span>UNLOCKED</span></h2>
                <p class="success-description">MEMORY SEQUENCE COMPLETE.</p>
                <div class="success-line"></div>
                <p class="success-footer">ACCESS GRANTED // TP-07</p>
              </div>
            </div>

            <div class="stage-bottom-label">
              <span class="tiny-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>
              <span id="stage-instruction">SYSTEM IN STANDBY</span>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="matrix-footer">
            <span>MEMORY TEST // TP-07</span>
            <span>SECURE CONNECTION // ESTABLISHED</span>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- RIGHT PANEL -->
        <aside class="mission-panel" aria-label="Memory protocol controls">
          <div class="mission-heading">
            <span class="heading-line" aria-hidden="true"></span>
            <h2>MEMORY PROTOCOL</h2>
          </div>

          <div class="level-display">
            <span class="label">LEVEL</span>
            <span class="level-number" id="level-count">01 / 07</span>
          </div>

          <div class="signal-message">
            <p class="signal-title" id="matrix-status">SYSTEM STANDBY.</p>
            <p class="signal-description" id="instruction">
              UNLOCK THE SYSTEM TO BEGIN.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="level-progress-section">
            <div class="progress-heading">
              <span>LEVEL PROGRESS</span>
              <span id="level-progress">00 / 07</span>
            </div>

            <div
              class="progress-track"
              id="progress-track"
              role="progressbar"
              aria-label="Completed levels"
              aria-valuemin="0"
              aria-valuemax="7"
              aria-valuenow="0"
            >
              <div class="progress-fill" id="progress-fill"></div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="mission-actions">
            <button class="text-button restart-button" id="start-button" type="button">
              RESTART TEST <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
            </button>

            <button class="text-button reset-button" id="reset-button" type="button">
              RESET PROTOCOL
            </button>

            <button class="unlock-game-button" id="unlock-game-button" type="button">
              UNLOCK <span aria-hidden="true">→</span>
            </button>
          </div>

          <p class="feedback-message" id="feedback" aria-live="polite">
            SYSTEM READY.
          </p>
        </aside>
      </section>

      <footer class="page-footer">
        <span>TP-07 // MEMORY TEST</span>
        <span>INTERACTIVE SYSTEMS DIVISION</span>
      </footer>
    </section>
  </main>
</body>
</html>